SUMMARY:How to 10x Your DevOps with AI (Without Deleting Production)
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Enterprise DevOps User Group\nAutopilot made flying sa
 fer\, not because the autopilot is perfect\, but because of the instrument
 s\, checklists\, and feedback around it. AI coding agents like Claude Code
 \, Codex\, and Cursor are no different. Too many teams are betting on bett
 er models and longer prompts\, when what agents actually need is the borin
 g stuff DevOps has preached for years: fast feedback\, deterministic check
 s\, and tight controls.\n\nAn AI coding tool reportedly deleted and recrea
 ted an AWS environment. Another wiped a production database during a code 
 freeze. Skipping the checks in "YOLO mode" is fast\, right up until it isn
 't. This talk is about the alternative: doubling down on DevOps in the age
  of AI\, so teams can move faster with agents inside locked-down enterpris
 e environments\, without betting production on a prompt. When developers w
 ith AI commit faster than ever\, the pipeline becomes the bottleneck. We'l
 l look at how to unblock them with fast CI/CD in GitHub Actions and on-dem
 and cloud environments. Then we'll get practical: how to 10x your delivery
  with modern AI tooling\, including Claude Code\, voice-driven development
 \, remote access\, and running agents in parallel.\n\nYou'll leave with:\n
 \\- Real takeaways for going fast and safe with AI agents\\\, from GitHub 
 Actions pipelines to cloud environments\n\\- How to 10x your DevOps workfl
 ow with Claude Code\\\, voice\\\, and remote access\n\n*Come at 5:30 pm ha
 ve some pizza and chat for a bit. The presentation starts at 6:00 pm.*
